  "body": "Found in the second safety read of PR #3140 (comment 7069305890).\n\nAfter PR #3140, a Contour with Arc entry and both leads set to None stands the wall arc down. The level then descends straight down. With a tool that is not centre-cutting, the operation is refused. The refusal is correct and safe. But its hint tells the user to \"pick the Arc entry\", and the user already has Arc entry.\n\nExpected: the hint names the real cause. The lead-in is None, so the arc entry does not run. The user can set a Linear or Arc lead-in, or use a centre-cutting tool.\n\nThe PR body of #3140 calls this a \"wording follow-up\". This issue tracks it. Change only the message text and its test. The refusal must stay.\n",
